            title: 'Kemps',
            subtitle: 'Partnership Signal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Kemps (also known as Kent or Cash) is a fast-paced partnership card game where teams try to collect four-of-a-kind and signal their partner to call 'Kemps!' The game involves secret signals, quick card exchanges, and trying to intercept opponents' signals.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Kemps is a relatively modern American card game that emerged in the 20th century. The exact origin is unclear, but it has been popular in the United States since at least the mid-1900s. The game is also known as Kent in some regions.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 4\nMaximum Players: 6+ (in teams of 2)\nOptimal Players: 4\nPartnerships: Yes (teams of 2, partners sit opposite)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Type: Standard 52-card deck (2 decks for 8+ players)\nNumber of Decks: 1 (or 2 for larger groups)\nJokers: No',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck\nTable space for 4 face-up cards',
              },
              {
